  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual claim and the visual of the Black child",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'once you go black ur a single mom!' and the visual material of the Black child being held, as the meme implies that the user (or anyone who becomes Black) is automatically associated with being a single mother. This projection is implicit, using the text to create a direct link between Black identity and single motherhood, which the user is expected to internalize as a universal truth. The child's visual presence reinforces this projection by making the stereotype feel immediate and personal.",
